# PostgreSQL Types, Constraints and Indexes

## Purpose

This document defines the SQL types, constraints and indexing strategy used in the Police Case Management System (PCMS).

## SQL Types

| Type | Usage |
|------|-------|
| BIGINT | Primary keys |
| VARCHAR | Short text |
| TEXT | Long text |
| BOOLEAN | Flags |
| DATE | Business dates |
| TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE | Audit timestamps |

## Constraints

### NOT NULL

Mandatory business fields.

### UNIQUE

- users.email
- roles.name
- departments.code
- cases.case_number

### CHECK

- file_size >= 0
- valid status values
- valid priority values

## Default Values

- deleted = FALSE
- enabled = TRUE
- created_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

## Indexes

- idx_users_email
- idx_cases_number
- idx_cases_status
- idx_case_assignments_case
- idx_case_comments_case

## Foreign Keys

The schema uses foreign keys with `ON DELETE RESTRICT` to preserve referential integrity.
